---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice - CUNY AI Lab">
  <PageHero containerClass="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-200">Interim notice · Version 2026-09-19-interim</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold font-display text-white tracking-tight">CUNY AI Lab Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/90">This notice explains how the Lab handles information across its services.</p>
  </PageHero>

  <main class="bg-white py-14">
    <article class="policy max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <p><strong>Effective September 19, 2026.</strong> This notice applies to the CUNY AI Lab website and the Lab services covered by the <a href="/terms/">Interim Terms of Use</a>.</p>

      <h2>Information the Lab receives</h2>
      <p>When you sign in, CUNY Login sends the Lab the identity information needed to connect your CUNY account to the services, such as your name, CUNY email address, affiliation information, and an account identifier. Access applications include the information you submit about your affiliation, campus, intended use, or class. The Lab also records access decisions, class membership, assigned allowances, API-key metadata, service events, and estimated model usage.</p>
      <p>The public website uses Google Analytics to understand how people use the site. The access form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check that a submission is made by a person. These services may receive standard web-request information, such as an IP address and browser type, and handle it under their own privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>Content stored in CAIL services</h2>
      <p>CAIL services may store content that you submit or generate as part of providing features such as chat history, projects, class spaces, and transcripts. Do not use CAIL as the only copy of important work.</p>
      <p>Administrators can access stored content when needed to operate, secure, or support the services. Other users can also see content you deliberately share with them, and your instructor and classmates can see content you post to a class space. Do not place sensitive personal or institutional data in the services unless CUNY has approved that specific use.</p>

      <h2>Model requests</h2>
      <p>Prompts, files, and model output pass through the Lab’s model gateway and are sent to external model providers to generate a response. The Lab selects and configures these services to limit provider retention and prevent user content from being used to train provider models. The gateway does not store prompts or responses, although a CAIL application may store content as part of the service it provides.</p>

      <h2>How information is used</h2>
      <p>The Lab uses this information to authenticate users, review requests, operate accounts and classes, enforce access and usage limits, provide support, secure the services, and understand service reliability and aggregate use. The Lab does not sell personal information or use user content to train or fine-tune models. Content is disclosed only as needed to provide, operate, secure, or support the services, or when disclosure is required by law.</p>

      <h2>Legal and institutional requirements</h2>
      <p>CAIL handles records in accordance with applicable CUNY policies and legal requirements. Because CUNY is a public institution, records may be subject to New York’s Freedom of Information Law, a subpoena, or another legal process, subject to applicable exemptions and protections.</p>
      <p>Contact <a href="mailto:ailab@gc.cuny.edu">ailab@gc.cuny.edu</a> with a privacy question or account request.</p>

      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>The version number at the top of this page tells you which notice you acknowledged. We will update this page when our services or policies change, and if a change requires your acknowledgement, we will ask you to review and accept the new version before you continue using the services.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .policy { color: #374151; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .policy h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: .65rem; color: #1D3A83; font-family: Outfit, sans-serif; font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .policy p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .policy a { color: #2A6FB8; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
